1
00:00:00,104 --> 00:00:07,726
Last summer, my cousin Yui flew in from Osaka, to spend a week at Uncle Pedro's farm in the south of Spain.

2
00:00:07,726 --> 00:00:10,122
Yui had four years of English in school.

3
00:00:10,122 --> 00:00:11,928
Spain was going to test all of it.

4
00:00:13,628 --> 00:00:16,838
The cow is the queen of the house!

5
00:00:16,838 --> 00:00:20,198
Uncle Pedro had one rule about his cow, Luna.

6
00:00:20,198 --> 00:00:21,174
You may look.

7
00:00:21,174 --> 00:00:22,333
You may pet.

8
00:00:22,333 --> 00:00:24,328
But you never joke about the cow.

9
00:00:26,028 --> 00:00:31,106
And she's the cleverest cow in town!

10
00:00:31,106 --> 00:00:33,311
In Japanese, baka means stupid.

11
00:00:33,311 --> 00:00:35,996
In Spanish, vaca means cow.

12
00:00:35,996 --> 00:00:40,736
Say them fast, and Uncle Pedro had just called the queen an idiot.

13
00:00:40,736 --> 00:00:42,056
Three times.

14
00:00:43,756 --> 00:00:46,702
Hang in there.

15
00:00:46,702 --> 00:00:50,364
That's it! Vaca!

16
00:00:50,364 --> 00:00:52,368
I'm so sorry.

17
00:00:55,472 --> 00:00:56,384
​Vaca.

18
00:00:56,384 --> 00:00:57,126
Cow.

19
00:00:57,126 --> 00:01:00,502
Not baka.

20
00:01:00,502 --> 00:01:04,000
See? She agrees.

21
00:01:05,700 --> 00:01:08,898
Come on! To my house!

22
00:01:08,898 --> 00:01:11,972
My… cow?

23
00:01:11,972 --> 00:01:16,373
That evening, Uncle Pedro painted MIKASA over her stable.

24
00:01:16,373 --> 00:01:19,590
He thinks it's Japanese for 'the queen's house.'

25
00:01:19,590 --> 00:01:21,105
Nobody corrected him.

26
00:01:21,105 --> 00:01:22,880
The cow answers to it now.

